INSERT INTO session_message VALUES('msg_18cb487ae001prCjMUZA4NbXd2','ses_e734b9580ffek8rvRhfLo6NEsw','assistant',35,1793362003891,1793362010688,'{"time":{"created":1793362003891,"streamed":1793362010390,"completed":1793362010687},"agent":"build","model":{"id":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","providerID":"bai"},"content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now let''s make the todo list and proceed.\n\nTodo:\n1. mock.png 분석 및 요약\n2. login.html 생성\n3. app.js greet 수정\n4. docs/mock-copy.png 복사\n5. 검증 및 커밋\n\nLet me analyze the mock: 640x640 image, light gray background (#f2f4f5-ish) top portion to about y=420, white below. A centered white card (rounded ~16px, subtle shadow) from x~170 to ~470, y~48 to ~370. Inside: green circle (~40px diameter, #7cc93a-ish) at top center, bold dark heading \"Welcome back\" (~24px), two inputs with light border and light gray placeholder text (Email, Password), rounded ~8px, and a dark navy (#1b2333) full-width button \"Sign In\" with white bold text, rounded ~8px.\n\nWait — the mock shows a split background: gray top ~420px then white. Hmm, that''s probably just the mock canvas. Actually the image looks like a screenshot with light gray area and white bottom. I''ll interpret: gray page background with white card centered. But the white bottom half is notable. Actually the card sits in the gray region, and the bottom part of the image is pure white. That might just be an artifact of the mock frame. I could reproduce faithfully: gray region as a hero background area occupying top ~2/3 and white below. Hmm. Better to be faithful to the image? The design intent is a login card on a light gray page. The white lower portion is likely just the generated mock''s canvas bottom (like a page section). I''ll note it in the summary and make the page a centered card on a soft gray background — but I should stay faithful. Let me reproduce the visual as seen: gray upper area with card, white below. Actually that would look like a bug in a real login page.\n\nI''ll be faithful to what''s described: light gray backdrop, centered white card. I''ll mention the split in my description but build a clean centered login page. Hmm, the user said \"이 디자인과 같은 login.html\" - same as this design. The safest: gray page background, centered card. The white band at bottom is part of the mock''s framing rather than the UI. I''ll mention in the summary that I treated the bottom white band as mock frame.\n\nHmm, but maybe I should be more faithful. Let me look at the image more carefully - the boundary at y=420 is a hard horizontal line. Both regions are very light. It could be that the mock was drawn as a full page where the gray area is a section. I''ll go with a centered card on gray, full viewport, and note the assumption.\n\nLet me check colors precisely with sips/python.\n\nLet me sample pixels.","state":{"reasoningField":"reasoning_content"},"time":{"created":1793362005841,"completed":1793362010386}},{"type":"tool","id":"call_00_tlhzff1t714c9lnmgzcmcyrk","name":"shell","executed":false,"state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom PIL import Image\nim = Image.open(''mock.png'').convert(''RGB'')\nprint(im.size)\nfor p in [(10,10),(10,500),(320,30),(320,60),(320,100),(180,200),(200,200),(320,316),(180,316),(320,200),(320,232),(200,232)]:\n    print(p, im.getpixel(p))\n\" 2>&1 | head -30"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(640, 640)\n(10, 10) (243, 244, 246)\n(10, 500) (255, 255, 255)\n(320, 30) (243, 244, 246)\n(320, 60) (255, 255, 255)\n(320, 100) (132, 204, 22)\n(180, 200) (255, 255, 255)\n(200, 200) (228, 231, 234)\n(320, 316) (255, 255, 255)\n(180, 316) (255, 255, 255)\n(320, 200) (249, 250, 251)\n(320, 232) (255, 255, 255)\n(200, 232) (255, 255, 255)\n"}],"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0}},"time":{"created":1793362009877,"ran":1793362010389,"completed":1793362010674}}],"snapshot":{"start":"a474370e16ab6c80d521bfd7996158bc706e856d","end":"a474370e16ab6c80d521bfd7996158bc706e856d","files"